  "provenance_html": "<p>Generator: Synthegra <code>main_v2.simulate_data_v2</code>, mode <code>pid_controlled</code> (commit 0f0dadd), two modalities with 40 features each from K = 8 latent factors, noise \u03c3 = 0.1, asymmetric unique weights (\u03b2 = 1.5 / 0.5), censoring 30 %. Synergy = strength of 2 planted cross-modal interactions between unique latent factors (<code>InteractionConfig.cross_modal_unique_pairs</code>); shared signal = fraction of latent columns loaded by both modalities (<code>PIDConfig.redundancy</code>).</p><p>Models, 3-fold stratified CV on held-out folds: best single layer = best of the two layers alone (boosted survival model or unimodal neural net); late fusion = per-layer boosted models, risk scores averaged for the C-index and survival curves averaged for the IBS; early linear = ridge-penalised Cox on the concatenated features; early non-linear = gradient-boosted survival model (150 trees, depth 2) on the concatenated features; intermediate = the best of three Synthegra neural intermediate-fusion architectures (simple sum, GMU, grouped Kronecker) \u00d7 hidden size 16 / 64, selected per cohort on the validation C-index and reported on the test folds. Oracle = C-index of the true linear predictor. IBS = integrated Brier score over 100 time points across the test fold's follow-up with Kaplan-Meier censoring weights (pycox EvalSurv), lower is better. Bars: mean over 8 seeds; whiskers: mean \u00b1 1.96 SD across seeds.</p><p>Why no redundancy / uniqueness / synergy read-out: the generator's quick built-in PID estimate reports substantial synergy on cohorts with no planted interaction, so it is not shown. The planted structure is exact by construction.</p>"
